      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2003-p5.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "2\nThe sphere's radius \\(r\\) satisfies \\(4 \\pi r^{2}=\\pi \\Rightarrow r=1 / 2\\), so the cube has body diagonal 1 , hence side length \\(1 / \\sqrt{3}\\). So, its surface area is \\(6(1 / \\sqrt{3})^{2}=2\\).",
